# Simson Line Theorem (classic test case)
# Let ABC be a triangle. Let P be a point on the circumcircle.
# Let D, E, F be the feet of perpendiculars from P to BC, CA, AB.
# Prove that D, E, F are collinear.

triangle A B C
circumcenter O A B C
on_circle P O A
foot D P B C
foot E P A C
foot F P A B
prove_collinear D E F
